That's the key.  If they're useful enough to be worth the weight, keep
them.  If not, ditch them.  If you've geno'd L, the book probably
goes.  If you have another light source and no far-range jumping
(expert in the spell), the candelabrum probably goes.  If you have a
couple /sdd (and maybe /opening, though they're less useful by now)
the Bell probably goes.

I often keep the candelabrum on to jump through the sanctum and use
the bell to find the door there, since they're already in main inv,
then drop 'em before the hike out.  If I'm planning on expert jumping
I'll turn off the candelabrum after doing the invocation and take it
to Astral w/ me.


